:
:>  QVSS (aka VCB01) is a single-board monochrome Q-bus graphics controller.
:>  The QVSS is not supported on most recent OpenVMS versions.
:
:I'm surprised.  A monochrome dumb frame buffer is pretty simple, and
:VMS has had much better support for old hardware than typical Unix OSes.

  Clarification: the console ROMs of this vintage simply didn't have room 
  for the console code for both the VCB01 and the VCB02 graphics controllers.
  Accordingly, adecision was made to remove the VCB01 in favor of the then
  newer VCB02.  If you configure the VCB01 at a (valid) non-default CSR, 
  use a serial console or a VCB02 as a graphics console, and then manually 
  configure the VCB01 under OpenVMS, you should be able to get DECwindows 
  to work on it.

