Everyone had a great time at DFWdays 2001... but it's the little things we'll
remember...
Hoff's 7.3 update, Advanced Server, TCP/IP,  Cluster Performance and Lock
Manager
Internals, The Galaxy Courses, Steve Stebulis's last minute substitution for
Rich Marcello
(Who got bumped  up into the  Vice Presidential stratosphere and couldn't make
it at the last minute)
and of course everyone's favorite Industry Pundit, Terry C. Shannon.

After it's all over it's the little things you take away from these events:

HAL calling to David Cathey about the AE-35 unit about to fail...
The DFWCUG's garish display of Nuclear Arms
CDroms with WAREZ  being passed around like WAREZ being pass around...
Building a Galaxy system from scratch.
Digital Network Product's wireless gateway to the Internet
Infoserver software that runs on  Alpha VMS.
HAL as one of the Judges for the DFWdays MAGIC Session
Digital India's Ad for OpenVMS Engineers (from which they hired 250!)
The Limited edition DFWdays 2001 Buttons
Jim Hibbit's / RAXCO's VMS Bigot Buttons
The  Life sized moonscape with a 1x4x9 Black Monolith lit by halogen lights
before sending a message to IO...
Raffling off two Arrows, one USB camera, a Digital Camera, gift certificates,
and a year's subscription to the Shannon Knows Compaq Newsletter
Mugs, BBQ Sauce, and versions of software that should never have seen the
light of day...

You could have been there...


And when it was  all over and HAL was quietly delivered to a manufacturer of
Console Management Software, somewhere in Plano Texas to care
for him  (after the nervous breakdown) and integrate him into their latest
