Jack Peacock wrote:
> I just acquired a decserver 90L+ with the password set on it, but no one
> knows what that password is.  Is there a way to restore a 90L+ to
> factory default in the same manner as the famous red button on a
> decserver 200?  I've pored over the user guide but found no mention of
> any way to restore factory defaults.

The method seems to be described on p 4-12 and p4-13
of the manual (EK-DSRVG-OM.001 DECserver 90L+ Owner's Manual).


The unit is permanently either in authorized mode
(i.e. there is a password required to affect other
ports etc.) or it is not.

To set authorized mode you do:
	SET,AUTH,S
now you get to enter a new password twice
(note that you do NOT enter the old password).

After doing this you must power-cycle within 60 seconds
to prove that you have physical access to the box.

You could do the above to set a password you *do* know.

Alternatively if you want to avoid the hassle of
a password at all you can clear the authorized mode
as follows:
	SET,AUTH,C
If you are already in manager mode (i.e. you have
previously entered the password) then authorized
mode is now cleared and the box will give you 
a message to that effect.
Otherwise you get told to power-cycle within 60 seconds.

Completely different to all the other DECservers
I've ever had the pleasure to manage.

(I've never managed a DS90L+, I'm just reading the manual
because I happen to have it to hand).

Antonio


