During Day One of the DFWDAYS meeting here in scenic Dallas Fort Worth,
the IBM-fabbed 1GHz Alpha EV68 microprocessor was revealed to all and
sundry. Since not everyone could attend DFWDAYS, candid photos of the chip
(in both pristine and de-lidded condition) may be viewed at former
Register reporter Mike Magee's new site at www.theinquirer.net.

The chip in question was extracted from an AlphaServer GS320
system. Benchmarks on the system are underway right now, and Compaq 
has plenty of the 1GHz (and, for that matter, faster) parts. Charlie Matco
informs me that the 1GHz WildFire upgrade will be announced next month. 

