Electric stoves and ovens in the US are typically 220 V, but single phase.
Three-phase vs. single-phase is not an effectiveness issue except for motors
and rectifiers (with single-phase, you need more inertia -- bigger flywheel
on the motor, bigger inductor or capacitor on the power supply filter -- than
with three-phase).  For heating, just raise the voltage to keep the current
reasonable for any given power level.  Cooking food surely doesn't care about
50 Hz vs 60 Hz (the power fluctuations, of course, would be at 100 Hz or 120
Hz, respectively).

                                RDP


