kch wrote:
> 
> Can anyone tell me what is required to transfer files from a VAXstation
> 3100-M76 to a PC? Assuming I could do something with the files once
> they're on the PC, the question is how do I hook the two computers
> together? The serial port on the VS3100 uses the offset RJ type
> connector, so I need to find a cable to go from this to the PC serial
> port. Surely other people have tried this.Or do I need to get an old DEC
> modem or something like that? I'd appreciate it if somebody could point
> me in the right direction.

You should also have a DB25 serial port on the back of it in addition
to the MMJ connectors. There are usually no parallel ports on the back
unless someone added a special interface to it.

If you have a DB9 connector on your PC, you can get DB9-DB25 converters
at almost any PC shop (watch the genders). You may also need a NULL
modem
(they are cheap, about $5 to $10 at PC shops). Get one of those RS-232 
line monitors (another $10, it's just some led's wired across intresting 
lines) to see if things are wired properly (when TXD and RXD are both
powered)
or when you need a null modem (only one of TXD, RXD is powered).

The MMJ connectors are simply a repackage of the RS232 signals into
a different connector (equivelent to pins 2,3,6,7, and 20 on db25)
To convert you just need cabling (no powered devices required),
but they are getting hard to find.

