:A friend of mine recently gave me two 3100s and a 2100.  I am wondering
:how I would go about attaching it to a MultiSync monitor, And if I can
:not, what monitor would I be on the look for that would work with it.

  I will assume that these are all DECstation 3100 and DECstation 2100 
  series MIPS-based systems (often running RISC ULTRIX), and not 
  MicroVAX, VAXstation, VAXserver 3100 series systems, nor DEC 2000 
  series systems.

  Systems of this vintage are very likely synch-on-green.  Details and 
  general tips and pointers on connecting synch-on-green monitors and/or
  graphics adapters assuming synch-on-green monitors are listed in the 
  OpenVMS FAQ.  (There is at least one adapter listed that permits the
  use of multi-synch monitors on synch-on-green graphics controllers.)

