The GFCI only monitors current on the "hot" and "neutral".  If they are
not the same, a fault condition is detected.  I understand the threshold
in the U.S. is about 5 mA.

Are you refering to GFCI breakers in a Circuit panel or the more local GFCI
protected outlets?

