James C.Geneva <jimgeneva@.qwest.net> wrote:
> Well I mostly would like to get it running for my computer collection. I
> usually like to get them running rather than just using them as very large
> paper weights.
> Web searching I have found out that I must get the monitor and keyboard that
> were
> made for it rather than trying to hook up a terminal to the RS 232 port which
> will not work and what of the OS called OS/278 that seems to be for it.

The keyboard is easy, you just need a LK201, the same keyboard was used for
a LOT of DEC hardware, and I wouldn't be to surprised if a LK401 keyboard
would work.  The Monitor is a bit trickier, as far as I know the same
monitor and cable was used on the DECmate II, DECmate III, DECmate III+,
Professional 325/350/380, and Rainbow.  I think it might have also been used
on the VT240 terminal.  Some of these systems also supported a Colour
monitor, but you want the Monochrome one.

To get the software on floppies you'll need a PC with a 1.2MB Floppy drive. 
I forget what software though.

				Zane


