Well, here in Sweden this is true when it comes to how it is wired in
the house. From the power company to your house/apartment you only have
4 wires: 3 phases and the neutral.


      main                      fuse            
     fuses                      box             VAX 6000
             ----------                       ------------
R ----|==|---|        |---------|==|----------|R         |
             | kWh    |                       |          |
S ----|==|---| meter  |---------|==|----------|S         |
             |        |                       |          |
T ----|==|---|        |---------|==|----------|T         |
             |        |                       |          |
N -----------|        |----------|------------|N         |
             ----------          |            |          |
                                 |------------|PE        |
                                              ------------

The incoming wires (at the left) are connected to the main fuses and
then to the kWh meter. From the kWh meter the wires are connected to the
fuse box. All power consumers in the house are connected to the fuse
box. In the wiring from the fuse box to the consumer neutral and
protective earth are separated, but they are connected in the fuse box.

Regards
   /Patrik


