Most residential power feeds are 220v single phase plus neutral. That is
what the three wires you see are. If you look inside your breaker box (kids,
don't try this at home! If you must look, go to your local home improvement
store and look at a new box.) you will find that alternating breakers are
supplied by each half of the 220 to neutral. If you need 220v you install a
double size breaker that fills two adjacent slots with 2 poles that clamps
on to both sides of the 220v distribution.

