If there are three wires coming into the house, then these would be
Ground/Neutral
and one of the three live phases. In western Europe there's no "two live
wires" left
in 220 volts systems.
Most houses are connected to all 5 wires (L1, L2, L3, N, G) but only one
live wire
is actually connected to the house system.

Note the big fuse on that single live wire: it is usually in a sealed box.
Don't trip it...

