Brian Chase wrote:
> 
> 
>   VAX 6000-600 CPUs     (check)
>   VAX 6000-600 RAM      (check)
>   XMI-2 card cage       (part number anyone?)
>   T2019 3.3V Power Reg  (Same as H7242?)
>   XBIA+ Module          (XMI half of the XMI<->VAXBI bridge?)
>   XTC Module            (What is this?)
> 
>   And then any necessary cables to hook this stuff together.

The above basically turns your XMI-1 chassis into
an XMI-2 chassis by changing all the bits that
are different between the two.

Except that if you go this route you *don't*
use the T2019 and you *do* use the H7242
(which replaces one the the H7214 IIRC).

You also get to remove lots of bits and replace
them with other bits.

If you want battery backup you may need to
do stuff with the H405 too.

The *easy* route is to pick up a T2019
from ebay or wherever. Make sure it comes with
the (blue?) powerbus cabling. The T2019 is
an XMI module like any other XMI module,
except it sits in slot 2 and blocks slot 1.

The upside is that you will have time for
a life. The downside is that you essentially
lose 2 slots and can support at most 4
KA65A or KA66A CPUs. Is this really
a problem :-) (Plus you cannot use
battery backup).

> I'm beginning to think it'll be cheaper to just freight ship the the whole
