Hello,

I have recently acquired a DECtalk DTC01 unit via eBay.  When powered on, a
fast sequence of DTMF tones is heard followed by "DECtalk version 2.0 is
running."  I'll take this as a good sign.  :-)

I need some assistance in identifying the connectors however:

On the back panel, there are 2 DB25 connectors.  The first is labelled COMM,
the second has what appears to be a video monitor symbol.  I'm assuming the
first connector is for a serial command sequence from a host and the second
connector is for some sort of serial console.

Next are 8 LED's - 1,2,4, and 7 are on.

Next are 2 telephone style jacks - the first is labelled with a telephone
handset icon, the next with a horizontal bar.  The first is obviously for a
phone line connection but I don't know the purpose of the second.

Next are 2 1/8" audio jacks - the first is labelled with an icon that
consists of a triangle pointing to the right inside of a square, the second
is labelled with a headset icon which I assume is for external audio to a
headset or other audio device.

Any assistance in identifying these connectors would be appreciated.

I have looked for documentation on the DCT01 using various search engines.
However, the only thing I could find was the following from Compaq:

EK-DTC01-HR    DTC01 (DECTALK) DOCUMENT. MAP           $5.00
EK-DTC01-IN    DECTALK DTC01 INSTALLATION MA          $21.00
EK-DTC01-IP    DTC01 DECTALK IPB                      $21.00
EK-DTC01-OM    DECTALK OWNERS MANUAL                  $21.00
EK-DTC01-PS    DTC01 (DECTALK) POCKET SVC GD          $42.00
EK-DTC01-RC    DECTALK DTC01 REFERENCE CARD            $5.00
