You are correct so far.  Connect a computer to the first port or a VTxxx
terminal
to the second port.

The default speed for the comm port is 1200, 9600 baud for the terminal
port.

You need a BC22D-xx or equivalent (null) modem cable.  I use office cables
and
adapters (BC16E-xx,H8575-A.  They work fine.

Standard phone cables will work for the phone jacks.  The DECtalk will
answer
the phone when programmed properly.

A break command on the second port will get you to a setup prompt where you
can
adjust baud rates, speech speeds and select voices.  This can be done from
the other
port too...

I have the installation manual and DECtalk; A Guide to Voice (sales
literature with
some technical content), but no spares.  Sorry.  I do have the ACT DECtalk
(VAX BASIC) demo software source code that is useful for programming
examples.
Let me know if you are interested and I'll send it.  It now runs on Alpha...

Regards,
Tom

