Hi Bernd,

Yes, I think I do. I've replaced 2 power supplies at a customer site
in the last 3 weeks. The DS700s had the symptoms you describe - 8 in
the display and the green LED on.

The power supplies output 3 voltages: 5V, -10V, and +12V. In my case
both the -10V and 12V outputs on both PS modules were OK. But both
5V outputs were 2.9v to 3.1V, which is enough to power the LEDS but
not enough to allow the control CPU to run.

When I metered each bad power supply without the cable connector
plugged into the DS700 circuit board, each 5V output measured 5V.

So my supplies will not supply 5V under load. Without a schematic
I haven't tried to troubleshoot the bad supplies but I suspect the
5V rectifier is a full wave bridge and one side has opened up.

Hope that helps,

Jeff Campbell
