Brian Chase wrote:
> 
> I've got a VAX 6000-420 and some CPUs coming from a VAX 6000-6xx system.
> Is it possible to replace the VAX 6000-4xx series CPUs with the VAX
> 6000-6xx CPUs?  If it is possible, is it just as simple as pulling out the
> old CPUs and swapping in faster ones, or does something more need to be
> done?
> 
> -brian.

More.  The VAX 62x0/63x0/64x0 used write-thru caches, while the later
65x0/66x0 used write-back caches.  If your 64x0 has original memories,
they will need to be replaced with later ones that had support for
write-back caches.

Also, maybe, if you have some early XMI I/O adapters, they may cause
problems.  Most of the I/O adapters were cured early enough that if
they shipped with a 64x0 they would also work with write-back CPUs.

There may also be some configuration constraints -- number of 6500
or 6600 CPUs comes to mind -- based on the older power supplies in
the 64x0.

Sorry I can't be more specific about the I/O and P.S. stuff, but the
memories are the primary concern.
-- 
Cheers, Bob


