daytripper wrote:
> So does Charlie find it ironic that all of the big Compaq SC wins are based on
> Clipper and Privateer boxen - and not Wildfire?

I am sure that Charlie would have been seriously surprised to see
GS being used in supercomputer configurations.

Supercomputing is typical about:
  - high FP performance
  - high FP performance/price
  - good tools/libraries/OS-support for parallelization

The GS series are more for the high-end business market, where it
is typical about:
  - reliability
  - server-consolidation
  - high INT performance
  - support from database and ERP vendors

The DS20 and ES40's are just more suitable for supercomputing building
blocks than GS's.

On the other hand I do not think you will see many banks prefer 8 ES40's
for a GS320.

Arne


