There is a system call, RPCC, Read Cycle Counter.

There is a "builtin" for DEC C that will give you
access to the counter, defined in builtin.h

At the moment I'm drawing a blank on which manual has
the documentation on this: I think it's in the
PAL code (I think I loaned the manual to someone).

Note that if you are running on a multi-processor
system you can get very strange results if you aren't
careful to check to see that the various counts you
pulled out and compared came from the same processor.
The counters are not synchronized between processors.

